course: dictionary
lesson: 1089
title: Bracken: a plant and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bracken is a large, tough fern. It grows thickly on hills, moors and in woods, and it is green in summer but turns brown in autumn. When you meet a word, look at the clues around it: a plant that grows on hills and changes colour with the seasons.
explain: «Badgers are very clean: they drag in fresh grass and bracken for bedding.» Bedding is what an animal lies on to sleep, so bracken must be a plant the badgers carry in to make a soft bed. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: "they drag in fresh grass and a large, tough fern for bedding" still makes sense.
explain: Watch for names too. «Bracken Cave in Texas holds about 15 million bats.» Here Bracken starts with a capital letter and names a place, not a plant. Capital letters and context tell you which meaning is in use.
fact: Bracken is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some bracken, not two brackens.
fact: Bracken means a large, tough fern that grows thickly on hills, moors and in woods.
fact: Useful phrases: a patch of bracken, hide in the bracken.
fact: In stories, animals hide in the bracken, and children make dens in it.
fact: Walkers push through bracken on hillsides, and it can hide ticks that may carry illness, so check yourself after a walk.
exercise: «Badgers drag in fresh grass and bracken for bedding.» What is bracken in this sentence? | A hole dug for toilets | *A large, tough fern | A type of bird | A kind of cave
exercise: «Walkers push through bracken on the hillside.» What does this suggest about bracken? | *It grows thick enough to be hard to walk through | It is a kind of rock | It is made of water | It only grows in the sea
exercise: «In autumn the hillside is covered in bracken.» What colour is the bracken in autumn? | *Brown | Pink | Blue | Bright white
test: «Bracken Cave in Texas holds about 15 million bats.» In this sentence, what is Bracken? | A type of fern | A dinner | A kind of bat | *A place name, the name of a cave
test: «A patch of bracken» means what? | *A small area where bracken grows | A kind of hat | A sleeping bat | A bundle of cut wood
exam: Jayden reads «animals hide in the bracken» in a story. What does this tell you about bracken? | It is a cave full of bats | It is only found in Texas | *It grows thick enough for animals to hide in | It is a kind of insect
